Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:58:09 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1121/1252] What waits, off its queue; the run from any room;
 regenerations seen at once (1165)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The engine's lamp opens what runs and what waits: this page's songs, the regenerations the lab queued (the engine's
log names a run only when it begins) and the lab's work on the cards; a waiting one comes off its queue by its ✕,
pressed twice; the list rebuilt only when what it holds changes (a button replaced under the pointer loses its
click). The context menu closes only on a scroll of what it was opened over (the log dock following its lines took
it away). The player's dot goes to the Creator before it shows the run or the take. The Librarian is read again when
the lab says it filed a regenerated or refined take. The artwork overlay's play is the cards' hollow one; fresh
cards' outline 1pt.

Translation groundwork: plural forms in a catalog entry, {#N} parts that take a number only, parts looked up in
turn; workspace, LoRA, font and repository names kept as typed (an <option> without a value is its own text); the
LoRA and VAE tiles translated piece by piece and drawn again when the language changes; the Trainer's epoch tips.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
